This is the unified visual overhaul contract (**`TDB-731`**) to transform the `Monaco` text editor into a true theater-grade **Karaoke Spotlight Spotlight**.

It implements five synchronized, high-performance visualization systems to guarantee that any active musical measure, track line, and note token in your `.ten` code literally leaps off the screen[cite: 1, 2]:

---

### What This Overhaul Adds

1. **Active Measure "Suburban Box" Spotlight (`tenuto-karaoke-measure-active`)[cite: 2]:**
* Real-time regex scan detects the entire text block of the active measure `measure N { ... }` in the code and wraps it in a glowing, dark-emerald-cyan box-glow with a vibrant left-side border and custom highlight-border corner brackets `[ ]`[cite: 2].


2. **"Inactive Measure" Opacity Fade/Dimmers (`tenuto-karaoke-subdued`)[cite: 2]:**
* Smoothly dims all lines outside of the active playing measure down to `28%` opacity[cite: 2]. The rest of the editor recedes, spotlighting ONLY what is currently being played.


3. **Dedicated Track-Line Pulse Indicators (`tenuto-karaoke-line-active`)[cite: 2]:**
* Highlights the precise track lines (e.g. `fpad: L158 [75%]`) with an active, pulsing emerald gradient and an animated gold highlight bar[cite: 2].


4. **Intra-Token Progress/Lyrics Sweep underlays (`tenuto-karaoke-token-active`)[cite: 2]:**
* Luminous gold-amber & emerald-green gradient text styling on active note/chord tokens with a progress overlay (`0% -> 100%`) showing exactly how much of a note's duration has played[cite: 2].


5. **Smooth Line Auto-Centering Scroller:**
* Uses smooth scrolling to keep the active measure positioned perfectly in the 1/3 top part of the viewport without abrupt jumps, keeping you focused during fast tracks.



